eXplore mode is the -X option, *not* the -D option.  It is true that a
game run as -D when you are not named "wizard" (or whatever the wizard
name is defined as in your particular binary) does start as eXplore
mode, but -D is not the correct option letter.

Notice the -[DX] below, showing that D and X are both options you can
pass.  D stands for Debug, while X stands for eXplore.

C:\nethack> nethack -?
 Usage:
 NetHack [-d dir] -s [-r race] [-p profession] [maxrank] [name]...
        or
 NetHack [-d dir] [-u name] [-r race] [-p profession] [-[DX]] [-n] [-
I] [-i] [-d]


